}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zendframework/zend-diactoros/deployments","created_at":"2015-05-21T16:48:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T13:13:27Z","pushed_at":"2020-01-29T15:09:57Z","git_url":"git://github.com/zendframework/zend-diactoros.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:zendframework/zend-diactoros.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/zendframework/zend-diactoros.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/zendframework/zend-diactoros","homepage":"","size":3656,"stargazers_count":1538,"watchers_count":1538,"language":"PHP","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":146,"mirror_url":null,"archived":true,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":29,"license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":146,"open_issues":29,"watchers":1538,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I'm not sure if this is intentional, but the current `CallbackStream` implementation is not compatible with `SapiStreamEmitter`. Because `CallbackStream` throws an exception on `rewind()` it cannot be combined with `SapiStreamEmitter`. A trivial example would be\n\n``` php\n$fp = imagecreatefrompng('/path/to/meme.png');\n$response = new Response();\n$response = $response\n  ->withHeader('Content-Type', 'image/png')\n  ->withBody(new CallbackStream(function () use ($fp) {\n    imagepng($fp);\n    imagedestroy($fp);\n  });\n\n$emitter = new SapiStreamEmitter();\n$emitter->emit($response);\n```\n\nIs there a reason that the `SapiStreamEmitter` is incompatible with `CallbackStream`, or should frameworks/applications be inspecting the response stream and choosing the correct em